            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0240" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60d2/11</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sayre</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-22">January 22, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In regard to the Finnish treaty the only thing that remains to be done is the
                    comparing of the Finnish and English texts by the Department. Arrangements are
                    now being made to obtain the services of a Finnish translator to do this work,
                    which may take several days.</p>
                <p>The Finnish Minister has already gone over the two texts and found a few errors,
                    which have been corrected. He has left with the Department his full power, and
                    consequently he is ready to sign the treaty as soon as we notify him that we are
                    ready.</p>
                <closer><signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] B. S[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ayre</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
